  "insights": [
    "Sellers stepped back faster than buyers. New listings fell 12.7% from September to 2,928, which kept inventory falling even as sales slowed to 1,592, and held months of supply just under four.",
    "Detached and semi-detached are the steady half of the market: detached is 0.7% below last October at $735,100, and semi-detached is actually up 0.8% at $685,200, with the tightest supply of any type at 3.16 months.",
    "Row and apartment homes carry the declines. Row is down 5.1% at $407,500 with 4.44 months of supply, and apartments are down 7.9% at $288,800, roughly 15% below their August 2024 peak.",
    "Detached prices still rose in two districts: City Centre at 3.3% and the West at 3.2%. The North East fell 6.6% and the East 6.8%.",
    "The softest corners are in the north and east: 9.47 months of apartment supply in the North, 8.60 in the North East, and 8.47 months of row supply in the North East.",
    "Outside the city, Okotoks remained the tightest at 3.04 months of supply, while Cochrane rose to 5.82 and Chestermere to 5.94. All four regional towns saw prices ease from September."
